<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD JATS (Z39.96) Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v1.0 20120330//EN" "JATS-archivearticle1.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">J Cell Biol</journal-id><journal-id journal-id-type="iso-abbrev">J. Cell Biol</journal-id><journal-id journal-id-type="publisher-id">jcellbiol</journal-id><journal-title-group><journal-title>The Journal of Cell Biology</journal-title></journal-title-group><issn pub-type="ppub">0021-9525</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1540-8140</issn><publisher><publisher-name>The Rockefeller University Press</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">6235233</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2275593</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="publisher-id">84264754</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Supplement: The Cytoplasmic Matrix and the Integration of Cellular Function</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Receptor-mediated transport of IgG</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Rodewald</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Kraehenbuhl</surname><given-names>J. P.</given-names></name></contrib></contrib-group><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><day>1</day><month>7</month><year>1984</year></pub-date><volume>99</volume><issue>1 Pt 2</issue><fpage>159s</fpage><lpage>164s</lpage><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; 1984, </copyright-statement><copyright-year>1984</copyright-year></permissions><abstract><p>The intestinal epithelium of the neonatal rat is a model system for thestudy of receptor-mediated endocytosis in which large amounts of IgG aretransferred intact across polarized cells. This review summarizes theultrastructural pathway followed by IgG during cellular transit and severalimportant properties of the membrane receptor that recognizes the IgG.</p></abstract></article-meta></front></article>